   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
  {
   "id": "el8_545140",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1656,
   "y": 214,
   "width": 542.88,
   "height": 427.5,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 1,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 126938844,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1775651416,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": null,
   "updated": 1795463233560,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "The UML arrow points AT the class you need first.\n• Triangle end (parent / interface)          → build first\n• Open arrowhead end (the class being used)  → build first\n• Diamond lines: the diamond sits on the WHOLE.\n  The whole needs its parts, so the end\n  WITHOUT the diamond is built first.\n\nSo the build edge is the UML arrow reversed:\n  UML   Child ───▷ Parent    →   Parent → Child\n  UML   Holder ───> Target   →   Target → Holder\n  UML   Whole ◆─── Part      →   Part → Whole\n\nHARD edge: dependent's header needs the full class\n  (base class, member by value, calls a method, new X)\n  → #include it, so it must already be written\nSOFT edge: only stores / passes X* or X&\n  → `class X;` (forward declaration) is enough\nHeader-only code: most edges are HARD, because the\nmethod bodies live inside the header.",
   "originalText": "The UML arrow points AT the class you need first.\n• Triangle end (parent / interface)          → build first\n• Open arrowhead end (the class being used)  → build first\n• Diamond lines: the diamond sits on the WHOLE.\n  The whole needs its parts, so the end\n  WITHOUT the diamond is built first.\n\nSo the build edge is the UML arrow reversed:\n  UML   Child ───▷ Parent    →   Parent → Child\n  UML   Holder ───> Target   →   Target → Holder\n  UML   Whole ◆─── Part      →   Part → Whole\n\nHARD edge: dependent's header needs the full class\n  (base class, member by value, calls a method, new X)\n  → #include it, so it must already be written\nSOFT edge: only stores / passes X* or X&\n  → `class X;` (forward declaration) is enough\nHeader-only code: most edges are HARD, because the\nmethod bodies live inside the header.",
   "fontSize": 18,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
